{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>Five and sixty and three hundred and a thousand.</b> So is the sum of the reckoning: five shekels per head — for the two hundred firstborn, a thousand shekels; for the seventy firstborn, three hundred and fifty shekels; and for the three firstborn, fifteen shekels. He said: How shall I do it? A firstborn to whom I say, 'Give five shekels,' will say to me, 'I am one of the redeemed of the Levites.' What did he do? He brought twenty-two thousand tickets and wrote on them 'son of Levi,' and two hundred and seventy-three tickets he wrote on them 'five shekels,' mixed them and put them in the calpi. He said to them: Come and take your tickets according to the lot (Sanhedrin 17)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:18.208502248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}